WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.470
- During the last days I was at home here

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:05.075
in North Rhine-Westphalia
in the west of Germany.

00:00:05.075 --> 00:00:07.070
Was really great to spend a couple

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:09.840
of days together with
my family, my sisters,

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.960
my parents, my wife, our baby girl,

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.640
just here at home recharging
the batteries a little bit.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.980
And just talking,

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.530
having some great
interactions with the family.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:24.390
Always, awesome and feels
like a little mini holiday.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.990
So I whilst thinking about the topic,

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.550
that I wanted to talk about today.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.590
And I remembered a
LinkedIn post that I wrote

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.230
a couple of weeks ago.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.990
By the way, feel free to follow
me on my LinkedIn as well.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:37.440
I will blend in my socials in here.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.600
But this post was about my twenties.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.330
So as you might know, at the moment,

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.330
I'm in my very early thirties.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.590
So my twenties are now behind me.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:49.533
And I was reflecting
what were the learnings,

00:00:49.533 --> 00:00:52.310
what were the lessons and insights

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.390
that I got out of my twenties.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:56.580
And because I did get
quite a lot of positive

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.520
feedback from you on the posts.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.870
I thought, let me expand on that

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.885
in a proper YouTube video.

00:01:02.885 --> 00:01:06.760
Because I felt like this post
was not even close to getting

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.480
into the details into everything

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.720
all my thoughts about this topic.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.300
And to provide a little
bit of context on my 20's,

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.640
let me just start by talking

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.030
about what my twenties were like.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.499
How all of this worked.

00:01:18.499 --> 00:01:20.740
And when I was about 19,

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:24.640
I finished high school
here in a rather rural area

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:25.890
in the west of Germany.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.690
In high school, I was always a solid,

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:29.260
but not a great student.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:31.070
I had a solid high school degree,

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.039
but not nothing extraordinary.

00:01:33.039 --> 00:01:35.910
But what I always knew
is that I was interested

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:38.350
in business and likely in the future,

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.480
I did want to work in business indeed.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.670
So I was looking for good
universities in Germany to study

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:47.540
business and preferably also
rather far away from home.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.720
Because I felt like this was
what I needed at the time.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.000
A new start, a new environment,

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.990
where I wanted to grow and study.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.400
So I decided for the university of Munich,

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.120
I always loved the city.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.800
The university seem great
and what's even better

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.520
is that this university offered

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.690
me the opportunity to
not only study business,

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.730
but also philosophy imperative.

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:12.710
This was a topic I was always
interested in during my youth.

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:15.460
And I felt like it was a
great opportunity to also have

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:17.983
exposure to this slightly different topic.

00:02:17.983 --> 00:02:20.680
Then I started two independent
bachelor's in parallel,

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.920
one in business, one in philosophy.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:23.800
So as you can imagine,

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.310
that was quite a special
and rewarding environment

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:27.270
as I found myself in.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.420
So surely the typical business student,

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.240
is a very different personality

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.600
than the typical philosophy student.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.610
In business we talked
about maximizing profit,

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:40.010
setting up in your
business in the best way.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:42.720
In my philosophy seminars,
it was not unusual,

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.040
that students starting to
debate whether communism

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.770
wouldn't be a great
form of society as well.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:51.360
Was also during the end
of my undergraduate degree

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.900
that I had the opportunity to
do the internship at McKinsey.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:55.740
And then after that,

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:59.250
I got the offer to join McKinsey
full-time as a consultant,

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.850
after my master, but I
did not even start yet.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:05.570
So clearly then it was
really a great feeling

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:08.070
to start in London at the
London School of Economics,

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.630
for this accounting and
finance master that I did,

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:13.770
already knowing that afterwards
I had the opportunity

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.290
to then join consulting,

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.600
which surely took a lot of
pressure out of my shoulders.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:19.700
So after my master,

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:22.330
I was 23 years old when I joined McKinsey,

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:23.960
first in the Berlin office.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:26.730
And I spent a couple of
years of working there

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:27.723
after this time in consulting.

00:03:27.723 --> 00:03:29.930
Which I think is very well documented

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.930
throughout all the videos on my channel

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.770
and then took the so-called
educational leave,

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.480
which usually the MBB firms offer.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:38.650
So this is a timer,

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:41.610
you can do an MBA or a PhD or even both.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:44.170
So this is the opportunity
that then I took as well.

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:47.193
I did my MBA at INSEAD
which surely was a great

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:49.210
and amazing experience as well.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:51.390
I spend half of the
time, roughly in France,

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:54.230
the other half of the time in Singapore,

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:57.290
using the opportunity
to travel through Asia.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:00.740
I remember like a two week
course that we had in China.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.730
I remember two week course that we had

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:05.020
in the Silicon valley,
where we all flew there.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:07.290
If you're interested to
hear more about that,

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.123
just write me a message.

00:04:08.123 --> 00:04:10.280
And I'll create maybe a future video,

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:13.330
where I just fully talk
about my MBA experience.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:14.163
After the MBA,

00:04:14.163 --> 00:04:16.980
I spent some additional
time working on my PhD,

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.070
and then I came back to McKinsey
to spend some additional

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.520
time working as a consultant.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:23.500
And this was then when,

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:25.940
at some point I was 28, 29,

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:27.890
were then I decided to leave McKinsey,

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:30.800
leave consulting started a medium sized,

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:33.370
retailer in Germany as a CTO position,

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.220
which is then where pretty
much my twenties ended.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:37.053
And now, as you know,

00:04:37.053 --> 00:04:40.750
this year transitioned to
even a new role as a CRO.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.490
So chief revenue officer

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.300
and a mature start-up here in Munich,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.940
which is what I'm currently doing.

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:47.560
So if you're interested more on that,

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:50.240
what a typical day in
this new role looks like.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.490
I recently created a video,

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.846
I will link it somewhere above here.

00:04:52.846 --> 00:04:55.210
Check it out to know
what this is all about.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:56.770
So I hope that this helps to give a little

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:00.290
bit of context of what my
twenties were all about,

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:03.220
but not before we dive
into what my lessons

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:04.390
and insights are,

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:06.670
what are the things are
that at least I hope,

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:09.020
might be helpful to some of you as well.

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:12.070
Let me first start by
properly greeting you here.

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:13.960
So welcome come to another coffee break

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:16.060
here on my channel Firm Learning.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:16.893
My name is Heinrich,

00:05:16.893 --> 00:05:19.190
and on my channel I want to help you,

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:23.090
to become successful in the
first years of your career.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.310
So for those of you who are watching

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:25.770
the first time, on my channel,

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:28.300
I talk a lot about
consulting related topics,

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.870
career topics, generally reflections

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.900
that hopefully help people probably

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:35.770
around the mid twenties
to maybe the mid thirties.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:38.480
To grow as a person and as a professional,

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.210
but now let's really dig into it.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:44.270
So what are the insights
that I got from my twenties,

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:46.840
from what happened to me in
the early parts of my life?

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.590
The first reflection I would
love to share with you is to

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.826
think about what the typical pathway is,

00:05:51.826 --> 00:05:55.010
that a similar person
like you will likely take.

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:58.190
And I think about how
you can actively expose,

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.730
yourself to rather unusual situations

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.610
and try out new things,

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:05.200
that most other people in your environment

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:07.060
will likely not have the opportunity

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:09.870
or will likely not have
the willingness to do that.

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:12.240
So think about that, what
will a typical person,

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.060
more or less similar to you likely

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.050
do at the start of their twenties.

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.790
Well very likely they
will move to another city,

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:21.300
start studying at university.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:24.220
Will put some time into
learn for the exams.

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:26.550
Try to write at least decent grades

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.480
or occasionally go out
with friends, go partying.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:30.910
Of course, have a good time.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:34.550
Maybe at some point do a semester
abroad than start a solid

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:36.700
job during the mid twenties or so.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:39.130
Then start earning some decent money

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:40.800
and then growing their career from there.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:44.660
So this is likely the baseline
of activities that you should

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:46.550
and will do in your twenties.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:48.580
And of course, I'm very
well aware that this

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:50.300
is very privileged already

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:51.640
and likely there will be many,

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.760
many people in the world who
do not have the opportunity

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.020
to do even this.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.540
So surely if you do this,

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:59.310
this is what likely the majority

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.750
of the people in your environment will do.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.370
And the result of that will be,

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:05.020
if you only do this,

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:07.660
that you will get more or less
the same things that all the

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.530
other people in your surrounding will get.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.330
I'm not saying that this is a bad thing,

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.245
but as I know that many
of you are very ambitious

00:07:14.245 --> 00:07:16.290
and do want to achieve maybe a little bit

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.660
more than the average of your peer group.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:21.610
Here are the key question that
you should ask yourself is,

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:24.140
what can I do on top of that?

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:27.860
What are experiences I can expose myself

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:29.830
that will add to my learnings,

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:33.340
add to my reflections will
help me really develop my

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:36.080
personality, develop myself as a person.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.910
So reflecting on my twenties,

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:41.610
I can only say that some of
the experiences that helped me

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.580
the most were exactly these experiences,

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.040
which were maybe a little bit unusual.

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:50.060
Maybe a little bit
leaving the beaten path,

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:52.080
to do some additional new things.

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:54.370
And in the show I already
talked about studying,

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:57.720
philosophy in my undergraduate
as an additional degree.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:07:59.500
This definitely was not something

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.160
that many other people did.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.355
Also decided by university studies,

00:08:03.355 --> 00:08:05.420
to join the student group.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.500
So in Munich there's the
so-called CDTM program,

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:11.730
Center for Digital
Technology and Management.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:13.440
It's an additional honors degree,

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:15.830
that you do on top of
your regular studies.

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:17.600
It's a lot about entrepreneurship,

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:21.210
building new projects,
developing products,

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:23.250
marketing them, doing sales for them,

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:24.970
how entrepreneurship works,

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:27.650
how you raise money for a start-up idea.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:29.700
This was all additional work.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.060
Lots of time, in my evening,

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:35.430
I probably invested at least
as much time in only this

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:39.270
specific honors degree, than
in my regular business degree.

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:42.130
But the learnings and insights
I got from them were so

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:44.860
tremendous and really helped me so much

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:46.630
in all the years after that,

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:49.230
that I would not have wanted to miss that.

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:51.580
What really also helped
me both personally,

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:54.420
but also professionally is to do as many

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:56.640
internships as possible.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:58.070
So during the semester,

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:00.850
I even skipped weeks
and months of lectures,

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:02.980
just to do additional internships,

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:05.020
expose myself to new situations,

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.650
working in new companies
and new environments.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:11.100
Some of them also abroad,
even in other continents.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:14.010
So clearly from that, I
did not only learn a lot.

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:16.100
It really also helped me develop myself

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:19.410
and surely this was then also
instrumental to the later,

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:22.190
for instance getting the
internship at McKinsey,

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:25.930
which then helped me to start
my career as a consultant.

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:28.170
On top of that, I would
argue that even starting

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.800
this YouTube channel early last year

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:34.320
is an example of doing
things off the beaten path.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:37.210
So clearly starting a YouTube
channel is not something that

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:39.380
everyone else in your environment will do.

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:41.780
I'm also not recommending
all of you to do this.

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:44.120
But for me, it just was a leap of faith,

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:46.160
earlier last year to do this,

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:48.130
I definitely learned so much,

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:50.870
just from producing these videos to you.

00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:54.270
And definitely this also
already opened up many

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:56.260
opportunities for me personally,

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:59.630
just by regularly
bringing these videos out

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:02.410
and hopefully adding some
value to you by doing that.

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:05.390
As you know, the famous Steve Jobs quote,

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:08.300
you can only connect the dots backwards.

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:10.590
Who knows what it will be good for,

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:13.890
if you follow a maybe exotic
hobby during university

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:14.940
or during your twenties,

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:15.800
the only thing that you know,

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:19.150
for certain like things
that you do not do will,

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:22.590
definitely not be able to
help you later down the road.

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:26.300
My second reflection is
on the value of your time.

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:29.176
So definitely at least most
people in their twenties,

00:10:29.176 --> 00:10:31.670
especially why they're
still at university,

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:34.990
but often also in the
more entry level careers,

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:37.150
especially if you're not
working in a high paced career

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:38.220
like banking or consulting,

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.910
you will like you have a lot of time.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:42.460
And if not during the day,

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:44.470
than at least in the evenings.

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:48.220
And here especially the time
that you have in the evenings,

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:51.130
I truly believe that how you use that.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:55.450
Will very much determine your
life in the next five years,

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:57.350
in the next 10 years.

00:10:57.350 --> 00:10:58.870
So think about the last days,

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:01.230
how do you use your time in the evenings?

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:04.720
And I know it can feel hard
after a long day at work.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.840
If you're coming home at 6:00 PM, 7:00 PM,

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:10.680
8:00 PM, 9:00 PM being at home,

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:12.320
you often feel exhausted.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:15.400
So surely it feels great
to sit in front of the TV,

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:18.940
to watch Netflix, to spend
time with your friends,

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:20.110
with your family.

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:22.470
And I'm not saying that
you should not do that.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:26.320
So clearly it is so important
to recharge your batteries,

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:27.986
spend time with your loved ones.

00:11:27.986 --> 00:11:30.570
This is definitely
something you should do.

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:32.000
Though this is just the truth.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.280
If every evening you sit at home,

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:37.300
watch Netflix, your life in five years,

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:40.610
your life in 10 years
will look very different,

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:44.160
compared to if you use the time
to do something productive,

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:47.940
maybe work on a side business
on additional like idea that

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:49.920
can maybe grow into something bigger.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.760
Maybe even just spend
time with a great hobby,

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:56.530
maybe you like photography,
maybe like videography.

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:58.410
And here it's not even necessary

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:01.050
to always have a big master plan

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:03.390
of what will come out of these things.

00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:05.040
So let's think about photography.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:07.270
Maybe you just started as a hobby

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:09.410
and then spend time in the evenings,

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:12.210
researching the topic, learning about it,

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:14.740
getting some experience in practice.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:16.020
But maybe then in the future,

00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:18.410
you develop this into
a little side business,

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:20.330
where you do photography for maybe

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:21.840
weddings or other things.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.790
And this is just an additional source

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:26.200
of side income that
you really enjoy doing.

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:28.110
Or maybe you start a YouTube channel

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:30.840
talking about your insights, your hobby,

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:32.150
what you learned from that,

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:33.990
and thereby helping other people.

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:37.520
Or maybe by learning about
the photography industry.

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:39.490
You suddenly have a business idea.

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:41.570
An idea for a start-up

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.050
that you can now develop

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:44.840
and now you can get yourself into.

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:46.840
And that might help you
to quit your regular

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:49.740
nine to five job and
become an entrepreneur,

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:51.680
create a business out of that.

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:54.940
So once again, it's not always
possible in that very moment

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:57.909
to know what certain
activities will be good for,

00:12:57.909 --> 00:12:59.760
later down the road.

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:02.617
The only thing that's certain
is that if you just spend this

00:13:02.617 --> 00:13:07.377
time watching Netflix and
movies, every single evening,

00:13:07.377 --> 00:13:10.627
surely here, nothing good
will come out of that.

00:13:10.627 --> 00:13:14.200
Surely this will not help
you, to improve your life,

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:17.360
five years, 10 years later down the road.

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:20.140
Last but not least let's
talk about investing.

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:22.680
So you hear one thing
I hear quite commonly

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:24.930
from people in their 20's is to say,

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:26.660
why should I save money?

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.900
It's much harder for me to save a little

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:30.640
bit of money right now.

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:32.930
Why shouldn't I just start saving money

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:33.840
and investing in my

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:36.020
thirties where I likely will have earned

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:38.284
much more money were likely than saving

00:13:38.284 --> 00:13:40.120
a little bit of my earnings,

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:43.020
will be much easier to me
than now in my twenties.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:45.738
Maybe still a student or in my first job,

00:13:45.738 --> 00:13:48.370
still I don't have a
lot of money it's just

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:49.860
so much more difficult.

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:51.960
And to be frank, I used to think like that

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:53.860
in my early twenties as well.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:55.350
But thankfully over time,

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.810
my mindset on this changed a little bit.

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:00.490
And I have two answers,
two replies to that,

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:02.410
if you think like that as well.

00:14:02.410 --> 00:14:05.120
The first is the value of habits,

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:07.120
the value of getting used to that.

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:10.020
So if you never really got any experience,

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:12.030
any habits in saving your money,

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:14.154
if you're just always spending it all,

00:14:14.154 --> 00:14:17.670
it will be extremely
difficult for you to suddenly

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:20.940
in your thirties to start
saving a substantial

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:23.854
amount of your income every single month,

00:14:23.854 --> 00:14:27.030
just to build your capital,
build your net worth.

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:29.890
This would be so much more
difficult to you instead

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:33.960
of if you even only with
small sums maybe 50 bucks

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:36.280
or so every single month, as a student

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:40.040
you are already putting aside
in an investment account

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:43.050
and then develop this habit
from a very early age.

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:46.330
But I would even object to the
second point that right now,

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:48.890
it doesn't even matter if you're only save

00:14:48.890 --> 00:14:51.250
and invest small amounts of money.

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:53.470
And what people here really underestimate

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:55.852
is the power of accumulating interests.

00:14:55.852 --> 00:14:59.610
And there are some really
mind blowing calculation,

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:02.400
examples out there to what an effect,

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:07.400
even saving small amounts of
money in your twenties can have

00:15:07.508 --> 00:15:10.560
to your long-term accumulation of wealth

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:12.630
and long-term accumulation of net worth.

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:14.610
Investing only small amounts of money

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:16.480
like a hundred or 200 euro,

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:19.170
every single month can really snowball

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:22.359
into much more significant
amounts later down the road.

00:15:22.359 --> 00:15:24.330
Or to put it differently,

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:27.450
if you compare the net worth
of someone who only starts

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:30.180
investing in his or her thirties,

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:32.090
compared to someone who starts already

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:34.170
investing in their twenties,

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:38.260
the amount of additional money
that the person in his or her

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:41.090
thirties needs to put into the savings

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:43.730
and investments account
every single month,

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:47.090
just to be on the same page
with someone who already

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:50.140
started investing in his or her twenties

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:51.680
is really mind blowing.

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:52.960
So there are lots of calculation,

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:53.820
examples like that.

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.700
I will link here about a video,

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:57.990
where I talk about the
importance of saving.

00:15:57.990 --> 00:16:00.180
Also share one of these examples.

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:02.480
Were I can hopefully have a
better understanding of that.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:05.590
If you doubt that if you doubt
that there is value in saving

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:07.810
even small amounts of
money in your twenties,

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:08.780
watch this video.

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.780
And I hope that this
convinces you to do otherwise,

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.280
